# Copy to repos.conf (git-ignored, keep it private) and adjust.
# Repos the sandbox may push to / open PRs/MRs against, via `agent-pr`.
# <host repo path> <github|gitlab> <host> <upstream slug> <base branch> <token file> [<push slug (fork)>]
# token file: mode 600, a token scoped to that one repo (see README). Used for git over HTTPS and gh/glab.

# GitHub, pushing directly to the repo:
/path/to/clone github github.com owner/repo main /path/to/home/.ssh/agent-pr/repo.token

# GitLab (self-hosted), pushing to your fork and opening an MR against upstream:
/path/to/other-clone gitlab gitlab.example.com group/subgroup/repo main /path/to/home/.ssh/agent-pr/other-repo.token your-user/repo
